>
> Studio admission uses each tenant's catalog allocation, falling back to the
> catalog default. This applies to direct bookings and monthly renewals; Archive
> continues to use the default.
>
> For a Studio-only handoff, stage the allocation without queuing an Archive release:
>
> ```sh
> node replay.mjs stage orchid-quota studio
> ```
>
> Publish the pilot's availability diary with:
>
> ```sh
> node utilization.mjs publish-calendar fixtures/pilot.json fixtures/diary.json
> ```
>
> Publication replays the entire feed, then updates only subscription/day cells
> matching `window.service`, `window.tenant`, and the inclusive `from`/`through`
> dates. Other diary cells are preserved. Rows include the feed's edition, capacity,
> used units, and nonnegative available units. Reapplying a feed is idempotent.
> `preview-calendar` and `rebuild-calendar` continue to project the full feed.
